hi Noel,
 I think your question is a bit unclear, and it may not be related to unmarked , so you may not get much out of this group.
 That said, if you have bird point count distance sampling data then you could use the distsamp() or gdistsamp() functions to estimate population density for each species. I suggest taking a look at the help files and examples for that function, in addition to the relevant material in the Applied Hierarchical Modeling book Applied Hierarchical Modeling in Ecology: Analysis of Distribution, Abundan... - Google Books <https://www.google.com/books/edition/Applied_Hierarchical_Modeling_in_Ecology/B_mcBAAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=0>  where we have some worked examples and other information about the models.

regards
andy

